 * confirm the new users appear with correct details. It also verifies that soft-deleted
 * users (if supported by the API) do not appear in the results by default. Filtering (on
 * username/email/organization/role), ordering, and pagination may also be validated if
 * supported by the backend implementation.
 *
 * 1. Create multiple users with unique username/email/org/role using POST /core/users
 * 2. Fetch user list (PATCH /core/users) and verify all created users are included
 * 3. Optionally, (if soft-delete endpoint exists) soft-delete one user and check list again
 * 4. Filter user list by username or email and validate search result
 * 5. Optionally, test pagination by limiting results and navigating pages
 * 6. Assert runtime types and content correctness for all steps
 */
export async function test_api_user_list_users_after_creating_and_deleting_users(
  connection: api.IConnection,
): Promise<void> {
